stack follows LIFO = Last In, First Out

Stack is a legacy class that extends Vector

public class Stack<E> extends Vector<E>

| Method      | Purpose                 |
| ----------- | ----------------------- |
| `push()`    | Add element on top      |
| `pop()`     | Remove top element      |
| `peek()`    | View top element        |
| `isEmpty()` | Check if stack is empty |
| `search()`  | Find element position   |

❌ It is synchronized (slow)
❌ Based on Vector (outdated design)
❌ Poor performance in many cases

instead of stack, use Deque (ArrayDeque) for better performance and more features.